\t}\n$$" 13194139535256 17592186045417 true] [17592186068489 1071 "Solve the equation $\\left\\vert 7x \\right\\vert = 21$." 13194139535256 17592186045417 false] [17592186068489 1071 "Solve the equation $\\left\\vert 7x \\right\\vert = 21.$" 13194139535256 17592186045417 true] [17592186068489 1074 "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $\\mid 7x \\mid = 7x$, we obtain:\n$\\mid 7x \\mid |= 21; 7x|= 21; \\frac{7x}{7}|= \\frac{21}{7}; x|= 3$\n- If $\\mid 7x \\mid = -7x$, we obtain:\n$\\mid 7x \\mid |= 21; - 7x|= 21; \\frac{-7x}{-7}|= \\frac{21}{-7}; x|=-3$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=3$ and $x=-3$. We can write this more compactly as $x = \\pm 3$." 13194139535256 17592186045417 false] [17592186068489 1074 "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|7x| = 7x,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|7x| & =21 \\\\ 7x & =21 \\\\ \\frac{7x}{7} & =\\frac{21}{7} \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|7x| = -7x,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|7x| & =21 \\\\ -7x & =21 \\\\ \\frac{-7x}{-7} & =\\frac{21}{-7} \\\\ x & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=3$ and $x=-3.$ We can write this more compactly as $x = \\pm 3.$" 13194139535256 17592186045417 true] [17592186068490 1071 "Solve the equation $\\mid 2x+9 \\mid = 15$." 13194139535256 17592186045417 false] [17592186068490 1071 "Solve the equation $| 2x+9 | = 15.$" 13194139535256 17592186045417 true] [17592186068490 1074 "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $\\mid 2x+9 \\mid =